[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583606747","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101372#issuecomment-2583606747","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101372","id":2583606747,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z_rXb","user":{"login":"Hiiamwilliam","id":62215077,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyMjE1MDc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62215077?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hiiamwilliam","html_url":"https://github.com/Hiiamwilliam","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hiiamwilliam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hiiamwilliam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hiiamwilliam/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hiiamwilliam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hiiamwilliam/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hiiamwilliam/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hiiamwilliam/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hiiamwilliam/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hiiamwilliam/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-10T18:57:52Z","updated_at":"2025-01-10T18:57:52Z","body":"I believe this is an issue about SceneTree priority and _maybe_ not a bug.\n\nThe Node that has state_controller.gd has a higher index (`get_index()`) than player_bad. \nI don't know the physics internals so I might be wrong, but I think that when the state controller will begin processing physics, player_bad already finished its processing physics. This could be why there's a delay: state_controller moves player_bad, but proper synchronization only happens on next physics process frame.\n\nNow, maybe there is indeed a bug in the sense that if the CharacterBody3D was moved through move_and_slide, its children should always have their position updated as well? No idea.\n\nRegardless, you can \"fix\" this in two ways: either move the state controller Node to have a lower index than player_bad (closer to root), or make its `process_physics_priority` higher than player_bad (by decreasing the value).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583606747/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585201459","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101372#issuecomment-2585201459","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101372","id":2585201459,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aFwsz","user":{"login":"vlap00000","id":142384974,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHyfTg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142384974?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlap00000","html_url":"https://github.com/vlap00000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlap00000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlap00000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlap00000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlap00000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlap00000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlap00000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlap00000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlap00000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlap00000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-11T10:50:19Z","updated_at":"2025-01-11T10:50:19Z","body":"I found a solution by enabling and disabling the move via a variable, without calling the move function itself. Not 